--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -13,6 +13,18 @@ You can find the details of how to do a Docker-based deployment in our [Docker d
 If you want more flexibility to customize your Fizzy installation by changing its code, and deploy those changes to your server, then we recommend you deploy Fizzy with Kamal. You can find a complete walkthrough of doing that in our [Kamal deployment guide](docs/kamal-deployment.md).
 
 
+## Language
+
+Fizzy defaults to English. Add `?locale=ja` to any page to switch to Japanese,
+or `?locale=en` to switch back. The choice is saved to your identity when
+signed in and applies across accounts and devices, including notification emails.
+If you choose a language before signing in, Fizzy remembers it for the session
+and saves it after you authenticate.
+
+When upgrading an existing installation, run the database migrations to add the
+locale preference to identities.
+
+
 ## Development
 
 You are welcome -- and encouraged -- to modify Fizzy to your liking.
