@@ -78,3 +78,22 @@ Under the hood, this will create or remove `tmp/email-dev.txt`.
 
 This gem depends on some private git repositories and it is not meant to be used by third parties. But we hope it can serve as inspiration for anyone wanting to run fizzy on their own infrastructure.
 
+
+## Localization
+
+The offered locales are configured in `config/application.rb`. The application
+catalogs in `config/locales` cover page copy, accessible names, mail subjects
+and bodies, time formats, and the small set of strings used by Stimulus. The
+`client` section is rendered into the page head; client-side dates use `Intl`
+with the document language, not the browser's preferred language. Keep user
+content, enum values, and URL parameters separate from translated labels.
+
+Mailers should render with `localized_mail` and the **recipient's** identity,
+not the language of the person or job that triggered the email. Shared page
+fragments and ETags already include the request locale.
+
+Two surfaces don't render through the normal app templates: static error pages
+in `public/` contain both languages, and the staff job console uses localized
+overrides of the Mission Control views in `app/views/{layouts/,}mission_control`.
+Check those overrides when updating the gem. The editor's bundled JavaScript
+strings belong to Lexxy.
